{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1290,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Airplane jet engines have gotten bigger and\nbigger over time - and it’s not just because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5810,
    "dDurationMs": 4901,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "planes are getting bigger: the Airbus A350\nis a smaller plane than the Boeing 747 but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10711,
    "dDurationMs": 1539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has bigger engines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12250,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The reason?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13290,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bigger engines are simply more efficient,\nup to a point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16390,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Modern jet engines actually consist of two\npropulsion systems working together: the jet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20660,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "core, which provides the power and a small\namount of thrust, and the fan, which is just"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24500,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a big propellor driven by the jet core that\nprovides most of the thrust."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28550,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pure jet engines can be incredibly powerful\n(which is why they’re used for fighter jets),"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33750,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they’re also horribly inefficient because\nthey shoot out their exhaust at super high"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37330,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "speeds, which equates to huge amounts of kinetic\nenergy, since kinetic energy is proportional"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41860,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the speed squared, so accelerating exhaust\nto twice the speed takes 4 times the energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46620,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In exchange for power, they literally blast\nenergy away as a bunch of hot air."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51130,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, you do have to shoot some air out\nof the back of an engine to generate thrust,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54930,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it doesn’t have to have lots of energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57150,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of accelerating a little bit of air\na lot, you can achieve your desired thrust"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60870,
    "dDurationMs": 4439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by accelerating a lot of air a little bit\n- you get the same momentum boost but save"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65309,
    "dDurationMs": 1291,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a ton of energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66600,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Essentially, if you make an engine too small,\nit has to accelerate the air so much as to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70710,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be a waste of energy – kind of like using\na machine gun to propel your car."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74640,
    "dDurationMs": 3650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you make the engine too big, then it\nstarts to cause too much drag."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78290,
    "dDurationMs": 4670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An ideal engine is somewhere in between – rough\nestimation puts the ideal engine somewhere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82960,
    "dDurationMs": 4870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around 4 meters in diameter, which is just\nslightly bigger than the current largest engines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87830,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can expect jet engines to continue\ngrowing in size... but not forever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92850,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I’d like to thank Audible.com for supporting\nthis video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97240,
    "dDurationMs": 3809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you may have heard, Audible has audiobooks\nof all sorts, including fiction, non-fiction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101049,
    "dDurationMs": 1221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and periodicals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102270,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can try Audible free for 30 days by going\nto audible.com/minutephysics, and if you do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106810,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so I recommend the book Ender’s Game by\nOrson Scott Card, it was one of the pivotal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111200,
    "dDurationMs": 3459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sci-fi novels I read as a teenager and I can’t\nrecommend it enough."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114659,
    "dDurationMs": 1931,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Remember, the enemy’s gate is down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116590,
    "dDurationMs": 5380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you can try Audible free for 30-days by\ngoing to audible.com/minutephysics."
    } ]
  } ]
}
